                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c95ea617-a2d8-3cda-9fc8-9d0c8a031ec6",
                        "entry_id": "4735429f-955b-3692-8a0a-5e966a0f5776",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A brakeman; a railroad employee responsible for a train's brakes, couplings etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5aa63018-b666-4ab4-b3fc-ea53fecefc9d",
                                "sense_id": "c95ea617-a2d8-3cda-9fc8-9d0c8a031ec6",
                                "text": "Leisurely we moved forward--reached the head of the train--then Andrews, Brown our engineer, and Knight, who also could run an engine, leaped on the locomotive; Alfred Wilson took the top of the cars as brakesman, and the remainder of us clambered into the foremost baggage car, which, with two others, had been previously uncoupled from the hinder part of the train."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f670ca5c-8c40-424a-8885-d96bc424617a",
                                "sense_id": "c95ea617-a2d8-3cda-9fc8-9d0c8a031ec6",
                                "text": "And some time after becoming naturalized, in one of his letters, he wrote that he was a brakesman on the Great Western R.R., (in Canada--promoted from the U.G.R.R.,) the result of being under the protection of the British Lion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55fdfcbb-f91f-44ce-8586-6829af73fda7",
                                "sense_id": "c95ea617-a2d8-3cda-9fc8-9d0c8a031ec6",
                                "text": "The young man on the ranch later said he was tenant in charge of the place for Mitchell Robertson, who owned it, but who was then working on the train as a brakesman out of Calgary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b98c964-9b54-478a-b8ee-3d0c22c659bc",
                                "sense_id": "c95ea617-a2d8-3cda-9fc8-9d0c8a031ec6",
                                "text": "[...] their speed (which was not supposed to exceed 10 m.p.h. normally, and less when the train was heavy or the weather was bad) was regulated by brakesmen known as \"bank-riders.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "017c0ca3-f7ce-434b-b8ca-c61a6c69d148",
                                "sense_id": "c95ea617-a2d8-3cda-9fc8-9d0c8a031ec6",
                                "text": "When the trains meet, the points of the loop are operated from the lineside by the trainmen or brakesmen specially carried for this job."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
